    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Specifically, vignette 21 should be helpful for finding a reasonable criterion.</div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"https://github.com/simsem/simsem/wiki/Vignette\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/simsem/simsem/wiki/Vignette&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792424708384000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1-jWWskBWcVG3VjO0BaiJR\">https://github.com/simsem/simsem/wiki/Vignette</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>Vignettes 24-28 show how to do model comparison with Monte Carlo, if that is also something you will need.</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"font-size:small\"><div style=\"font-size:13px\">Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div style=\"font-size:13px\">Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics</div><div style=\"font-size:13px\">Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div style=\"font-size:13px\"><a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792424708384000&amp;usg=AOvVaw199zwS3jNgrs_F90aB2R9r\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div><div><br></div></div></div></div>"
